+
+
+### Semantic clock ownership
+
+Phase lifecycle timestamps, credit issuance, replay scheduling, branch timers,
+and Worker request records use aiperf.common.clock. Its default provider
+delegates to Python's real clock. An internal simulator can use
+clock.use_clock(provider) with an event loop on the same timeline; the
+provider is scoped to that execution context and its child tasks. This leaves
+the native HTTP transport and unrelated task contexts on their real clocks.
+The simulator must settle request registration and callback delivery before
+advancing its timeline. A clock provider alone does not virtualize asyncio
+timers or replace the replay state machine.
